    "A physically finite connected C superlevel component has a highest plateau Q that is locally maximal in the full plane. Q has a WHITE incident collar. The signed finite prepared-plateau theorem therefore supplies an essential first-L curve in Q, impossible for a finite physical set. Nonzero drift aliases cannot bypass this: intersecting connected superlevel components with a nonzero translate would coincide and force infinitely many physical faces. At zero odd output only, exact time reversal is also WHITE and supplies the dual no-finite-L-sublevel principle.",
    "The independently signed contact barriers at arbitrary sheetj confine any inside C>=j+1 component, or at zero output any inside L<=j-2 component, to the bounded disk. The no-finite-component principle consequently forces all inside C<=j and, in the zero-output case, all inside L>=j-1. This is not an assertion about essential circles or homology cancellation.",
    "Fresh30-history78-sheet reconstruction gives98 canonical turns:44LEFT,52non-singletonRIGHT,2singletonRIGHT. EachLEFT has higherC>=j+1; eachnon-singletonRIGHT has lowerL<=j-2. The singletonRIGHT exception has bothL=j-1 and is an actual odd output, hence absent at zero output. Literal unchanged L1/L3 and both exchange transitions are included.",
    "At a LEFT corner the two C sectors connect through its geometric RIGHT patch. In the only possible same-sheet doubleLEFT smoothing the central complementary patch joins both C sectors, so a second visit to the same primal cell cannot evade this placement. Likewise RIGHT has both L sectors on its LEFT, with central L connection for doubleRIGHT. These are physical rounded embeddings, not unsmoothed graph intersections.",
    "A clockwise contractible circle has bounded interiorRIGHT. AnyLEFT corner would putC>=j+1 inside, contradiction. All corners thereforeRIGHT; its Jordan turning number requires exactly4 quarter-turns/edges. Since physical ports are unit grid edges, it is an elementaryC-face loop, and support plus the disk bound gives Cheightj. This part needs no zero-output premise.",
    "At zero output a counterclockwise contractible circle has interiorLEFT and no singletonRIGHT. AnyRIGHT corner would putL<=j-2 inside, contradiction. AllcornersLEFT, hence exactly4edges around an Lface; support and the disk bound force Lheightj-1. Nonzero drift can create short quotient aliases but a contractible lift is a genuine finite Jordan curve, so the argument stays physical."
